# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Big files.
#
# The model and the database ARE shipped, through git-lfs, so that a clone can
# run the app straight away instead of retraining a model first. See
# .gitattributes for what LFS handles and README.md for the fallback if the
# free LFS bandwidth runs out.
#
# The training CSVs are NOT shipped: ~206MB, only needed to retrain, and every
# one of them is downloadable or regenerable from the scripts here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The trained DistilBERT lives in git-lfs (255MB, over GitHub's 100MB limit).
# Rebuild if ever needed: train_reading_model_v3.ipynb on Colab, then
# tune_cutoff.py. Its working scores file is not worth shipping:
analyzer/reading_model/mcintire_scores.csv

# The old TF-IDF word-counter, only used when the reading model is missing.
# Rebuild: python train_honest_model.py
analyzer/model.pkl
analyzer/vectorizer.pkl
analyzer/model_meta.json

# Training and test data, ~206MB.
#   Fake.csv, True.csv          ISOT, from Kaggle
#   fake_or_real_news.csv       McIntire -- THE EXAM
#   diverse_fakes.csv           python fetch_diverse_fakes.py
#   diverse_reals.csv           python fetch_diverse_reals.py
*.csv

# db.sqlite3 is shipped through git-lfs (106MB). Rebuild: python load_mega_data.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordinary Python and editor noise
